  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Caballero's two-homer night broke a 4-1 tie in the fifth and held firm from there.",
    "what_this_means": "Schlittler gave them a pristine foundation. Eight innings, one run, eight strikeouts. But the offense was strangled until Caballero arrived in the right moment. Seventeen strikeouts in a 5-1 win is not a formula that scales. What matters is that one player converted the one real opening the game offered, turning what could have been a pitching duel into breathing room. They needed that margin because consistency is still the problem. The streak flipped from L2 to W1 today, and the division gap closed by one game. But this team doesn't win clean. It wins when someone shows up to finish what the pitcher started. Caballero showed up. The rest found nothing.",
